rrent.name` but not `current.archived`, so a case archived mid-pass can still be named. Cheap hardening: treat `current.archived` like gone (remove the candidate and continue).", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/run/definition_seed.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Some index updates are inert: the carried.add after a fill or a create, and the candidates.remove after a fill", "recommendation": "none. Corpus case names are unique per template (SeedCorpus validator, definition_seed.py:411). So `revision.carried.add(case.name)` at :977 and :1121 can never stop a later corpus case of the same pass. `candidates.remove(candidate)` after a fill is masked by the re-read: the twin test passes with it deleted. Harmless defensive bookkeeping, and no edit is wanted.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/run/definition_seed.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Docstring prose: _fill_empty_name still says 'case of ``template``' after that parameter was removed, and the _StoredRevision docstring cites (#1148)", "recommendation": "instance; NOTE-grade prose. In the first line of _fill_empty_name (definition_seed.py:1062), say 'of the revision'. Delete the '(#1148)' citation from the _StoredRevision docstring (:1002), since issue and review ids don't belong in shipped comments. The 'why' sentence stands without it.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/run/definition_seed.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "No recorded test evidence (test-status: no .test-evidence.json)", "recommendation": "none. This is the inner stage, so it is not a finding. The builder reports 60 passed on test_definition_reset.py, and that the counting test fails on the old code (5 queries vs 1). Record the evidence before the boundary review.", "oid": "O-5"}], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "no-claim", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims 